{
  "$comment": [
    "Urdu digits use EXTENDED Arabic-Indic (U+06F0-U+06F9), not Arabic-Indic",
    "(U+0660-U+0669). The blocks look identical for most digits but four, six",
    "and seven are drawn differently: Urdu uses \u06f4 \u06f6 \u06f7 where Arabic uses",
    "\u0664 \u0666 \u0667. Using the wrong block is a silent, easy mistake that produces",
    "digits an Urdu reader will not recognise.",
    "",
    "Every name from eleven upwards is its own word rather than a compound:",
    "Urdu does not build 47 out of 'four' and 'forty' the way English nearly",
    "does, so \u0633\u06cc\u0646\u062a\u0627\u0644\u06cc\u0633 has to be written out, and so does every other one.",
    "They were authored by hand and want reading by a native speaker - see",
    "todo.md. What is shown at once is capped by a band in Settings; see",
    "activeNumbers() in src/lib/content.js."
  ],
